{"record": "end", "run_id": "20261116T081736Z_dev-05_flat_bd76", "reason": "answered", "detail": "", "answer": {"answer": "The paper does not report a detection significance (σ or TS) for the GCE in its 17.7-year analysis. It says only that the fitted GCE flux is nonzero in all 80 diffuse-emission models, and states that this alone does not establish its statistical significance. It reports only goodness-of-fit values for DM spectra fitted to the GCE spectrum (e.g. χ²_min = 27.50 for 12 dof for b b̄) and Δ(−2lnL) differences between diffuse-emission models. It notes these model differences cannot be read as Gaussian significances because the models are not nested.", "found": false, "evidence": [{"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.5"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "3.4"}, {"arxiv_id": "2610.26648v1", "section_id": "6.1"}]}, "turns": 2, "seconds": 7.121, "tool_calls": 1, "tool_result_chars": 147086, "input_tokens": 6, "output_tokens": 730, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 65530, "cache_read_input_tokens": 1883, "parser_versions": ["4"], "response_models": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"], "ended_at": "2026-11-16T08:17:44+00:00"}
